      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Backend Development using Nodejs + Express\n\nBefore actually getting started with Backend development\nlets actually first lean how the web works\n\n->lets understand with a example suppose we want to visit a \nwebsite which is on the internet ,the steps we follow are :\n\n1.goto your favrouite browser like chrome,eddge,brave,arc or firefox\n\n2.enter the URL (universal resource locator) that is we specify the\nscheme,subdomain ,domain and top level domain or in other word\nin search engine we type a host name and we press enter\n\nsuppose we vist www.acedemind.com \n\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Backend Development using Nodejs + Express\n\nBefore actually getting started with Backend development\nlets actually first lean how the web works\n\n->lets understand with a example suppose we want to visit a \nwebsite which is on the internet ,the steps we follow are :\n\n1.goto your favrouite browser like chrome,eddge,brave,arc or firefox\n\n2.enter the URL (universal resource locator) that is we specify the\nscheme,subdomain ,domain and top level domain or in other word\nin search engine we type a host name and we press enter\n\nsuppose we vist www.acedemind.com \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
