      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Chapter2:HTTP/HTTPS ,understanding client side and sevrer side with request \nand response object\n\n ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Chapter2:HTTP/HTTPS ,understanding client side and sevrer side with request \nand response object\n\n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "bi2vEB2z29JX5btTNf0PT",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 537.1796642188699,
      "y": 27892.12549950312,
      "width": 1841.3994140625,
      "height": 405,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bN8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 564164707,
      "version": 7,
      "versionNonce": 1584551309,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730174632948,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "HTTP Hyper Text Transfer Protocol \nso what is a http and how does it play an important role in backend applications \n\nSo Http stands for Hyper Text Transfer Protocol as u can see its in the name that it is \nbasically a Protocol that is a set of rule to Transfer hyper Text which are basically html\npages ->so we can conculde at a high level that http is a Protocol which binds a set of rule \nfor machine to communicate or specifically for website ie client to communicate with server\nie http allows frontend to communicate with backend\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "HTTP Hyper Text Transfer Protocol \nso what is a http and how does it play an important role in backend applications \n\nSo Http stands for Hyper Text Transfer Protocol as u can see its in the name that it is \nbasically a Protocol that is a set of rule to Transfer hyper Text which are basically html\npages ->so we can conculde at a high level that http is a Protocol which binds a set of rule \nfor machine to communicate or specifically for website ie client to communicate with server\nie http allows frontend to communicate with backend\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "yeM3aQqpvif1RaFq4VXOe",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 549.988767309543,
      "y": 28401.97437326454,
      "width": 2039.399169921875,
      "height": 1035,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bN9",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 127538765,
      "version": 15,
      "versionNonce": 670915661,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730174711545,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Web document or client ------------------>sends a request that get this document like html \npage and styling sheet to render site to backend---->Server\n\nWeb document or client<---Sends html page and styling script after receving the request \nfrom frontend-----Server\n\n\nClients and servers communicate by exchanging individual messages (as opposed to a stream of data). \nThe messages sent by the client are called requests and the messages sent \nby the server as an answer are called responses.\n\nSo Http is basically a handshake protocol which means that client sends a request and \nrecives a response from server establishing a handshake\n\n\nFrontend or the client is what user interact with the  user interface created by using html css js and \nreact is what serves as frontend \n\nBackend are what the frontend interacts with mere user do not have the authority to interact \nwith backend untill and unless a backend engineer or a engineer is involved in the process \nbackend host server and database its written in js,java,python,golang,rust,c or c++\n\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Web document or client ------------------>sends a request that get this document like html \npage and styling sheet to render site to backend---->Server\n\nWeb document or client<---Sends html page and styling script after receving the request \nfrom frontend-----Server\n\n\nClients and servers communicate by exchanging individual messages (as opposed to a stream of data). \nThe messages sent by the client are called requests and the messages sent \nby the server as an answer are called responses.\n\nSo Http is basically a handshake protocol which means that client sends a request and \nrecives a response from server establishing a handshake\n\n\nFrontend or the client is what user interact with the  user interface created by using html css js and \nreact is what serves as frontend \n\nBackend are what the frontend interacts with mere user do not have the authority to interact \nwith backend untill and unless a backend engineer or a engineer is involved in the process \nbackend host server and database its written in js,java,python,golang,rust,c or c++\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
