      "seed": 57587629,
      "version": 198,
      "versionNonce": 1567020109,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730174766519,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "HTTP Protocol\nIn the end, its the client throwing some information at a server\nServer doing something with that information\nServer responding back with the final result\nThink of them as functions, where\n1. Arguments are something the client sends\n2. Rather than calling a function using its name, the client uses a URL\n3. Rather than the function body, the server does something with the request\n4. Rather than the function returning a value, the server responds with some data",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "HTTP Protocol\nIn the end, its the client throwing some information at a server\nServer doing something with that information\nServer responding back with the final result\nThink of them as functions, where\n1. Arguments are something the client sends\n2. Rather than calling a function using its name, the client uses a URL\n3. Rather than the function body, the server does something with the request\n4. Rather than the function returning a value, the server responds with some data",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
