      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730178340593,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "But one thing we have to understand is when we search for www.google.com we are actually hitting a\ncheckpoint www.google.com/ now here this / points to root directory where google is being served but since\ngoogle host many other websites and app on it server likr  gmail ,meet, and classroom etc so if we want to\naccess them one way is to directly use domain name like via searching gmail.com or other way is to use route\nlike we can say hmm first goto www.google.com and then at its root directory find gmail->for this we use\nroute like :\nwww.google.com/gmail/",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "But one thing we have to understand is when we search for www.google.com we are actually hitting a checkpoint www.google.com/ now here this / points to root directory where google is being served but since google host many other websites and app on it server likr  gmail ,meet, and classroom etc so if we want to access them one way is to directly use domain name like via searching gmail.com or other way is to use route like we can say hmm first goto www.google.com and then at its root directory find gmail->for this we use route like :\nwww.google.com/gmail/",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
