      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730178661004,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "So routes are nothing but a way to navigate to directories or domain to get the site hosted on\nserver,its very similar to terminal routing ie changing directory or going back one directory\nlet see :\n\n1.open terminal-I am gonna use git bash\n2.Change the route from parent directory or root directory to another drive or folder in our\ncase lets say we change it to D drive",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "So routes are nothing but a way to navigate to directories or domain to get the site hosted on server,its very similar to terminal routing ie changing directory or going back one directory let see :\n\n1.open terminal-I am gonna use git bash\n2.Change the route from parent directory or root directory to another drive or folder in our case lets say we change it to D drive",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
