    {
      "id": "csP8PRL7fHrBwjmC9p8jF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 727.7311295955456,
      "y": 80003.96863698364,
      "width": 2290.5816915239675,
      "height": 585,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bOu",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1909945613,
      "version": 166,
      "versionNonce": 1621273507,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730179435740,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is an API header?\nIn the context of REST APIs, headers are a part of the HTTP request that contain additional information about the\nrequest. Headers are used to provide additional information about the request, such as the format of the request\nbody, the client's preferred language, authentication credentials, and more.\n\nHeaders are included in every HTTP request and are used to provide additional information to the server about the\nnature of the request, or to provide additional context for the response. The headers can be used to specify a wide\nrange of information, including the format of the request body, the preferred language of the client, the type of\nresponse expected, and more.\n\nHeaders are key-value pairs, where the key is a string that describes the type of information being provided, and\nthe value is the actual data being provided. Some common headers used in REST APIs include \"Content-Type\",\n\"Accept\", \"Authorization\", and \"User-Agent",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is an API header?\nIn the context of REST APIs, headers are a part of the HTTP request that contain additional information about the request. Headers are used to provide additional information about the request, such as the format of the request body, the client's preferred language, authentication credentials, and more.\n\nHeaders are included in every HTTP request and are used to provide additional information to the server about the nature of the request, or to provide additional context for the response. The headers can be used to specify a wide range of information, including the format of the request body, the preferred language of the client, the type of response expected, and more.\n\nHeaders are key-value pairs, where the key is a string that describes the type of information being provided, and the value is the actual data being provided. Some common headers used in REST APIs include \"Content-Type\", \"Accept\", \"Authorization\", and \"User-Agent",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "23G-f6SyUT-Fi4ZDlkIyc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 735.8448644982551,
      "y": 80729.58739538777,
      "width": 2047.1619888856321,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bOv",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 791917773,
      "version": 148,
      "versionNonce": 402844941,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730179457820,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Headers are an important part of REST API design, providing a way to include additional information\nabout the request and response, and to control the behavior of the API.\n\n\n\nLet see the header request in action go to any website for our use case lets go to chat gpt and type a\nrandom question lets say : what is use of aysn in js hit enter and let the chat gpt do its work",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Headers are an important part of REST API design, providing a way to include additional information about the request and response, and to control the behavior of the API.\n\n\n\nLet see the header request in action go to any website for our use case lets go to chat gpt and type a random question lets say : what is use of aysn in js hit enter and let the chat gpt do its work",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
