    },
    {
      "id": "sZsFfl2fj2YapkfvqM2AJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 651.668766314109,
      "y": 98832.80840752006,
      "width": 1468.777244932534,
      "height": 765,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQ5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 360489517,
      "version": 420,
      "versionNonce": 660431565,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730180446601,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Question at this point - How do I create a HTTP server of my own? How to I\nexpose it over the internet like chatgpt.com\n\n\nHow do we write and http server -there are many ways to write an http\nsever we can write in c/c++,java using spring boot ,js using express ,go\nlang yada yada yada\n\nNow since we are focusing on MERN stack we will go with js and js \nprovide us a native module and 3rd-party framework that is node:http and\nexpress.js but what is express.js  we will see first\n\nwe will see how to create a server using node:http and then express.js\nand then we will discuss why we should use express over node:http:\n\nnode:http is a native module that is a code written by somebody else just\nlike fs module",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Question at this point - How do I create a HTTP server of my own? How to I expose it over the internet like chatgpt.com\n\n\nHow do we write and http server -there are many ways to write an http sever we can write in c/c++,java using spring boot ,js using express ,go lang yada yada yada\n\nNow since we are focusing on MERN stack we will go with js and js \nprovide us a native module and 3rd-party framework that is node:http and express.js but what is express.js  we will see first \n\nwe will see how to create a server using node:http and then express.js\nand then we will discuss why we should use express over node:http:\n\nnode:http is a native module that is a code written by somebody else just like fs module",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ybSRmqP9GW2BB7rmzxl5p",
      "type": "image",
      "x": 633.2569135670362,
      "y": 99633.27032911101,
      "width": 1172.2997610562093,
      "height": 685.9200729584203,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "transparent",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQ6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 425703363,
      "version": 69,
      "versionNonce": 759621091,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730180459676,
      "link": null,
