    },
    {
      "id": "1qASlzB6lfsbS1JoBYSQ9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 670.1166355950568,
      "y": 100601.05079767236,
      "width": 1286.99951171875,
      "height": 495,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQ7",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1460490061,
      "version": 376,
      "versionNonce": 65501475,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730184117137,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "So in nodejs we have to manually create a server using modules \nunlike language like php comes with tools to set up a sever like \napache server\n\n\nSo in nodejs we actually write or type code to create a server\nand listen in for the request comming from the browser and then \ndecide what to send in response \n\n\n ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "So in nodejs we have to manually create a server using modules \nunlike language like php comes with tools to set up a sever like \napache server\n\n\nSo in nodejs we actually write or type code to create a server\nand listen in for the request comming from the browser and then \ndecide what to send in response \n\n\n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "496j8SA_4mtb_RFStileM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 596.9863885734298,
      "y": 101304.27204063743,
      "width": 1405.999267578125,
      "height": 1305,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQ8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1228917859,
      "version": 923,
      "versionNonce": 309182691,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730184677723,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "so we will be using node:http module which comes with a createServer()\nmethod which creates a http server \n\nwe will be using ESM:\n\nimport {createServer} from \"node:fs\";\n\n//now this createServer-->takes a callback function as an argument\n\ncreateServer(function(req,res){}); \n\n//now createServer take a callback function and that call back function\n//has two argument 1.req object and 2.response object\n\n\n//now this request(req)->object comes loaded with full of request \n//information such as the url which is being requested ,request type \n//if its a get or post request\n\n//and response object is to respond to the browser\n\nconst server = createServer((req, res) => {\n    console.log(\"Request sent)\n});\n\n\nserver.listen(3000,\"localhost\",()=>{\n    console.log(`listening at port ${port}`);\n});",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "so we will be using node:http module which comes with a createServer()\nmethod which creates a http server \n\nwe will be using ESM:\n\nimport {createServer} from \"node:fs\";\n\n//now this createServer-->takes a callback function as an argument\n\ncreateServer(function(req,res){}); \n\n//now createServer take a callback function and that call back function\n//has two argument 1.req object and 2.response object\n\n\n//now this request(req)->object comes loaded with full of request \n//information such as the url which is being requested ,request type \n//if its a get or post request\n\n//and response object is to respond to the browser\n\nconst server = createServer((req, res) => {\n    console.log(\"Request sent)\n});\n\n\nserver.listen(3000,\"localhost\",()=>{\n    console.log(`listening at port ${port}`);\n});",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
