    {
      "id": "5jnqeyhQ443aJMPAX2Q49",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1975.012317050564,
      "y": 134778.87082408904,
      "width": 1108.999267578125,
      "height": 810,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bRH",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1069238723,
      "version": 873,
      "versionNonce": 176151587,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730228813223,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now here this createServer(cb) takes a \nrecursive callback that is when we hit a new route \nlike \"/\" createServer() will call the recursive callback\nand will extract the method associated with the route ,\nurl of the page \n\nwhen we will hit \"/submit\" route it will call the cb\nagain with request and response object basically \nand then manually will try to collect data using the \n.on() event handler which get's initiated on incomming \ndata  \n\nand if there was other route let's say /about \nwhen we will hit that route also then createServer()\nwill call that recursive call back\n\nso very thing method check and collection of \nincomming data happens in this recursive call back  ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now here this createServer(cb) takes a \nrecursive callback that is when we hit a new route \nlike \"/\" createServer() will call the recursive callback\nand will extract the method associated with the route ,\nurl of the page \n\nwhen we will hit \"/submit\" route it will call the cb\nagain with request and response object basically \nand then manually will try to collect data using the \n.on() event handler which get's initiated on incomming \ndata  \n\nand if there was other route let's say /about \nwhen we will hit that route also then createServer()\nwill call that recursive call back\n\nso very thing method check and collection of \nincomming data happens in this recursive call back  ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ZJhZlD0TnpYVt5p6SGtJX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 563.9832516864317,
