    {
      "id": "PcA4yJjl2IaG_qnukqCfW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1690.629418641471,
      "y": 136642.3268347617,
      "width": 1465.198974609375,
      "height": 765,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bRL",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1483134541,
      "version": 985,
      "versionNonce": 1886846979,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730230133696,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In express.js although express.js is built on top of node:http\nthe route handlers we get in express.js does not take a recursive \ncall back taht app.get(\"/\",(req,res=>{res.send(\"Hello\");});\n\nthis arrow function call back (req,res) is only associated \nwith \"/\" route it wont call it self for /submit route ,cause \nfor /submit route we have a different call back with req and res\nobject which have different functionality\n\nso when ever we hit a route the callback attached to that route/method\nget invoked only\n\n\nand to collect incoming request message from client we have middleware\nlike express.json or bodyParser() which are recurisve in nature that \nis very time a new route is hit they roload the server from top to bottom \nand catch incoming request",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In express.js although express.js is built on top of node:http\nthe route handlers we get in express.js does not take a recursive \ncall back taht app.get(\"/\",(req,res=>{res.send(\"Hello\");});\n\nthis arrow function call back (req,res) is only associated \nwith \"/\" route it wont call it self for /submit route ,cause \nfor /submit route we have a different call back with req and res\nobject which have different functionality\n\nso when ever we hit a route the callback attached to that route/method\nget invoked only\n\n\nand to collect incoming request message from client we have middleware\nlike express.json or bodyParser() which are recurisve in nature that \nis very time a new route is hit they roload the server from top to bottom \nand catch incoming request",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
