      "seed": 1792746861,
      "version": 45,
      "versionNonce": 1024450829,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730247038963,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Serving an HTML file using both createServer() from the Node.js http module and Express is straightforward. \nHere’s how to do it with each approach.\n\n1.Using createServer()\nHere's how to serve an HTML file using Node.js's built-in http module:\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Serving an HTML file using both createServer() from the Node.js http module and Express is straightforward. \nHere’s how to do it with each approach.\n\n1.Using createServer()\nHere's how to serve an HTML file using Node.js's built-in http module:\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
